  {
    "date": "2024-08-02",
    "term": "珍しい",
    "kana": "めずらしい",
    "meaning": "unusual, rare",
    "level": "N4",
    "pos": ["adjective (keiyoushi)"],
    "priority": ["ichi1", "news2", "nf33"],
    "pitch": [4],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": ["derivation"],
    "headline": "Mezurashii ultimately comes from the verb 愛づ (medu), whose descendant 愛でる (mederu) means “to love; to admire”.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From classical -na adjective 珍(めずら) (mezura) + しい (-shii, adjective-forming suffix)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Ultimately from Old Japanese verb 愛づ (medu, medzu), modern Japanese 愛でる (mederu, “to love; to admire, to appreciate”)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "The meaning originally referred to something that was admirable or favorable, something that had value, as an extension of the underlying verb. This meaning is used in the Man'yōshū, dating to the mid-700s. This further extended to indicate something that was rare or unusual in ways that one would find notable or attractive, and this meaning was also already used in the Man'yōshū. Over time, the admirable sense weakened, and the rare sense became dominant."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Cognate with Northern Amami Ōshima 珍っさり (むぃずぃらっさり, mïzïrassari)."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "id": 119616,
        "ja": "彼が怒るのは珍しい。",
        "en": "It is rare for him to get angry.",
        "enId": 284046,
        "form": "珍しい",
        "furigana": [
          ["彼", "かれ"],
          ["が"],
          ["怒", "おこ"],
          ["るのは"],
          ["珍", "めずら"],
          ["しい。"]
        ]
      },
      {
